import AFTD.Prelude

/-!
# is_convex_polygon_slack_matrix

Topic: integer_programming   Node: 8d4d3ce6b62c

Provenance: formalization of a published result. Source: arXiv:2610.04498 Sec. 2

A real matrix S : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ is the slack matrix of a convex n-gon in the plane (is_convex_polygon_slack_matrix n S) if 3 ≤ n and there exist an injective function v : Fin n → Fin 2 → ℝ and a family of affine functionals ℓ : Fin n → (Fin 2 → ℝ) →ᵃ[ℝ] ℝ such that the extreme points of the convex hull of range(v) equal range(v), the affine span of range(v) is ⊤, the convex hull of range(v) equals {x | ∀ i, 0 ≤ ℓ i x}, for each i there exist distinct indices j₁ ≠ j₂ such that ℓ i (v j₁) = 0 and ℓ i (v j₂) = 0, and S i j = ℓ i (v j) for all i and j.
-/

/-- A real matrix S is the slack matrix of a convex n-gon in ℝ² if it is generated by n extreme vertices and n facet-defining affine functionals. -/
def is_convex_polygon_slack_matrix (n : ℕ) (S : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℝ) : Prop := 3 ≤ n ∧
  ∃ (v : Fin n → Fin 2 → ℝ) (ℓ : Fin n → (Fin 2 → ℝ) →ᵃ[ℝ] ℝ),
    Function.Injective v ∧
    (convexHull ℝ (Set.range v)).extremePoints ℝ = Set.range v ∧
    affineSpan ℝ (Set.range v) = ⊤ ∧
    convexHull ℝ (Set.range v) = {x | ∀ i, 0 ≤ ℓ i x} ∧
    (∀ i, ∃ j₁ j₂, j₁ ≠ j₂ ∧ ℓ i (v j₁) = 0 ∧ ℓ i (v j₂) = 0) ∧
    ∀ i j, S i j = ℓ i (v j)
